  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.10: Targeted fixes on top of preview.9's concurrency hardening. INTEROP: PqJwtBearerHandler accepted the Authorization scheme as case-sensitive (\"Bearer \" only), in violation of RFC 9110 §11.1 (\"auth-scheme tokens are case-insensitive\") — requests with `Authorization: bearer ...` or `Authorization: BEARER ...` were rejected as no-result. The prefix check now uses StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase. SAMPLES: samples/VerifierDemo was broken by preview.9's HttpPqJwtKeyRing IHostedService refactor — it never registered the hosted service or called PreloadAsync, so /verify failed with UnknownKeyId on every request. Refactored to the canonical preview.9+ pattern (singleton + hosted service + DI in bearer options) plus SocketsHttpHandler PooledConnectionLifetime=2min for DNS-TTL honouring. CODE QUALITY: samples/PqJwtPlayground now caches its validator instead of building a new one per Validate() call (was triggering its own PQJWT002 anti-pattern). PqJwtBearerHandler's dead validator cache simplified — the per-instance reference-equality short-circuit never fired because auth handlers are transient. Tokens produced by this library's builder are unaffected; the public API surface for token issue/validate is unchanged. Production-oriented preview: NOT independently audited, NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
